From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: aiueo52 <aiueo52@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 15:11:01 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 054/105] hc boundary: compute the combine gate at mix time
 (SGLANG_HC_GATE_EARLY)

The HC combine's gate depends only on `normed_residual` and the fixed inject
weight, yet today it runs after the block output is ready, so its launch sits
on the boundary's post-block critical path (2.0 us x 102 boundaries/step at
W4, 2.2-4.8 us x 126 at W16, prod-0905 traces).

Two modes, both leaving only the apply stage after the block:

* FUSED (=1): the HC mix K0 branch CTAs already hold the normed row, so each
  one dots its branch slice against all HC inject rows and leaves one partial
  per (row, branch, gate). No gate kernel is launched at all. The reduction
  runs over branches instead of the gate kernel's 8 strided splits, so the
  gate value is not bit-identical (same fp32 accumulation, different order).
* MOVED (=2): the same split gate kernel, launched right after the mix.
  Bit-identical values; only its position in the stream changes.

The apply stage becomes its own JIT export whose partial count is a runtime
value, so it takes either layout. It also carries the (unused here) shared-
expert fold that the next commit turns on. Default off; the default path is
byte-identical to today.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
